  "answer": {
    "text": "Large enterprise sales organizations overwhelmingly rely on a few dominant platforms built to handle massive data volumes, complex hierarchies, multi-layered approval workflows, and deep security governance.\nThe primary CRMs used at this level include:\nSalesforce (Sales Cloud / Agentforce): The undisputed market leader and default standard for large global enterprises. It is chosen for its unmatched ecosystem, deep customization capabilities, complex territory management, and robust enterprise-grade security.\nMicrosoft Dynamics 365 Sales: The primary competitor in large enterprises, heavily favored by organizations already deeply embedded in the Microsoft enterprise ecosystem (Azure, Office 365, Teams, and Power BI).\nOracle and SAP: : Historically deployed in massive legacy conglomerates—often tightly integrated with enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems (like SAP ECC/S/4HANA or Oracle Cloud ERP)—though they are less common as pure \"sales-first\" choices compared to Salesforce.\nHubSpot (Sales Hub Enterprise): While historically a mid-market favorite, HubSpot has increasingly made inroads into larger organizations that prefer a more user-friendly interface and unified data model over the heavy implementation costs of Salesforce.",
